00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:54.000
you know, these people are breaking this tax law, or they're probably violating this regulation. But look, let's just leave it for the moment. It's sometimes slightly jokingly pointed out as one of the reasons why India didn't take off at the same time, because same size of market, huge entrepreneurship. But sometimes people say that essentially, India had too much red tape on the economy, and China had maybe not enough. But the short term effect, certainly in China, was to let the economy essentially go rip. And in the 1980s, we saw the effect of that in terms of the rapid growth that was seen in China's domestic market and also its capacity to export to the rest of the world. Ron, you mentioned this idea of jumping into the sea as an important metaphor in this period.

